course: dictionary
lesson: 14240
title: Neatness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Neatness is a noun. It means being tidy, clean and well arranged. It comes from the word neat, and the ending -ness turns it into a thing you can name, like kindness.
explain: At school, teachers often talk about neatness. They may look at your handwriting, how you present your work, or whether your desk is tidy. «Work on the neatness of your writing» is a helpful comment in a school report.
explain: Neatness shows in how things are set out. «Her neatness made her homework easy to read.» Here neatness means her work was clean, tidy and well arranged, so it was simple to follow.
fact: Neatness means being tidy, clean and well arranged.
fact: Neatness is a noun, and it comes from the word neat.
fact: At school, neatness is often about handwriting, presentation and tidy desks.
fact: Neat work is easy to read and easy to check.
fact: «Work on the neatness of your writing» is a sentence you might find in a school report.
exercise: «Her neatness made her homework easy to read.» What does neatness mean here? | Being late every day | Being very loud in class | Being good at football | *Being tidy, clean and well arranged
exercise: Your teacher writes, «Work on the neatness of your writing.» What should you work on? | Writing in red pen only | *Making your handwriting tidy and clear | Running faster at break | Drawing bigger pictures
exercise: Which thing shows neatness? | A desk with books piled in a heap | A bag with the zip broken | A page covered in messy scribbles | *A desk with pencils in a tidy row
test: What is neatness? | Being sad or tired | *Being tidy, clean and well arranged | Being very old | Being fast and loud
test: Mia's pens sit in a straight line, her books are stacked, and her bag is zipped. What does this show? | Hunger | Sadness | Noise | *Neatness
exam: Which sentence uses neatness correctly? | The paper was torn and muddy, which showed its neatness. | The dog had neatness in its bark. | He ran fast with great neatness. | *Her clean, straight writing showed great neatness.
